# Frontend configuration. Normally nothing needs to be set.
#
# The app calls /api/v1 on its own origin. In production that origin's edge
# Worker forwards /api to the API; under `npm run dev` and `npm run preview`
# Vite forwards /api to ATUS_DEV_API_ORIGIN (default http://localhost:8000),
# so no CORS setup is needed.
#
# Copy to .env.local for machine-specific development overrides. Production
# builds (`npm run build`) and tests read NO .env files: set build variables in
# the environment of the build command instead.

# Where `npm run dev` / `npm run preview` forward /api (not part of the bundle).
# ATUS_DEV_API_ORIGIN=http://localhost:8000

# Only to call an API on a different origin: an absolute URL, no trailing
# slash (the client appends /api/v1). That API must then allow this frontend's
# origin via ATUS_API_CORS_ORIGINS. A build fails if this is set to anything
# but an absolute http(s) URL.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000
